{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 11 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 11 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nMr. Chanek has an integer represented by a string $$$s$$$. Zero or more digits have been erased and are denoted by the character _. There are also zero or more digits marked by the character X, meaning they're the same digit.Mr. Chanek wants to count the number of possible integer $$$s$$$, where $$$s$$$ is divisible by $$$25$$$. Of course, $$$s$$$ must not contain any leading zero. He can replace the character _ with any digit. He can also replace the character X with any digit, but it must be the same for every character X.As a note, a leading zero is any 0 digit that comes before the first nonzero digit in a number string in positional notation. For example, 0025 has two leading zeroes. An exception is the integer zero, (0 has no leading zero, but 0000 has three leading zeroes).\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 11 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class P1575D {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n\n        String token = br.readLine().trim();\n        char[] s = token.toCharArray();\n        int ans = 0;\n\n        if (s.length == 1) {\n            if (s[0] == '0' || s[0] == '_' || s[0] == 'X') {\n                ans = 1;\n            }\n        } else {\n            int n = s.length;\n            if (!(s[n - 1] == 'X' && s[n - 2] == 'X')) {\n                // put 25\n                if (canPut(s, n - 1, '5') && canPut(s, n - 2, '2')) {\n                    char[] s1 = s.clone();\n                    put(s1, n - 1, '5');\n                    put(s1, n - 2, '2');\n                    ans += possible(s1);\n                }\n                // put 50\n                if (canPut(s, n - 1, '0') && canPut(s, n - 2, '5')) {\n                    char[] s1 = s.clone();\n                    put(s1, n - 1, '0');\n                    put(s1, n - 2, '5');\n                    ans += possible(s1);\n                }\n                // put 75\n                if (canPut(s, n - 1, '5') && canPut(s, n - 2, '7')) {\n                    char[] s1 = s.clone();\n                    put(s1, n - 1, '5');\n                    put(s1, n - 2, '7');\n                    ans += possible(s1);\n                }\n            }\n            // put 00\n            if (s[n - 1] == 'X' && s[n - 2] == 'X') {\n                char[] s1 = s.clone();\n                put(s1, n - 1, '0');\n                ans += possible(s1);\n            } else if (canPut(s, n - 1, '0') && canPut(s, n - 2, '0')) {\n                char[] s1 = s.clone();\n                put(s1, n - 1, '0');\n                put(s1, n - 2, '0');\n                ans += possible(s1);\n            }\n        }\n        pw.println(ans);\n        pw.close();\n    }\n\n    private static boolean canPut(char[] s, int p, char d) {\n        return s[p] == 'X' || s[p] == '_' || s[p] == d;\n    }\n\n    private static void put(char[] s, int p, char d) {\n        if (s[p] == 'X') {\n            replace(s, d);\n        } else {\n            s[p] = d;\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static void replace(char[] s, char d) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n            if (s[i] == 'X') {\n                s[i] = d;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static int possible(char[] s) {\n        int p = 1;\n\n        if (s[0] == '0') {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        if (s[0] == '_') {\n            p *= 9;\n        }\n        for (int i = 1; i < s.length; i++) {\n            if (s[i] == '_') {\n                p *= 10;\n            }\n        }\n\n        return p;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class P1575D {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n\n        String token = br.readLine().trim();\n        char[] s = token.toCharArray();\n        long ans = 0;\n\n        // Try all possible endings for divisibility by 25: 00, 25, 50, 75\n        String[] endings = {\"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"};\n        \n        for (String end : endings) {\n            char[] s1 = s.clone();\n            boolean valid = true;\n            \n            // Check if we can place the ending digits\n            if (s1.length >= 2) {\n                if (!canPlace(s1, s1.length - 2, end.charAt(0))) {\n                    valid = false;\n                }\n                if (!canPlace(s1, s1.length - 1, end.charAt(1))) {\n                    valid = false;\n                }\n            } else if (s1.length == 1) {\n                // For single digit, only \"0\" is valid for divisibility by 25\n                if (end.equals(\"00\") && canPlace(s1, 0, '0')) {\n                    valid = true;\n                } else {\n                    valid = false;\n                }\n            } else {\n                valid = false;\n            }\n            \n            if (valid) {\n                // Place the ending digits\n                if (s1.length >= 2) {\n                    place(s1, s1.length - 2, end.charAt(0));\n                    place(s1, s1.length - 1, end.charAt(1));\n                } else if (end.equals(\"00\")) {\n                    place(s1, 0, '0');\n                }\n                \n                // Check for leading zeros\n                if (hasLeadingZero(s1)) {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                \n                // Count possibilities\n                ans += countPossibilities(s1);\n            }\n        }\n        \n        pw.println(ans);\n        pw.close();\n    }\n\n    private static boolean canPlace(char[] s, int p, char d) {\n        if (p < 0 || p >= s.length) return false;\n        if (s[p] == '_') return true;\n        if (s[p] == 'X') return true;\n        return s[p] == d;\n    }\n\n    private static void place(char[] s, int p, char d) {\n        if (s[p] == 'X') {\n            replaceAllX(s, d);\n        } else {\n            s[p] = d;\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static void replaceAllX(char[] s, char d) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n            if (s[i] == 'X') {\n                s[i] = d;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static boolean hasLeadingZero(char[] s) {\n        if (s.length == 1) {\n            return false; // single digit 0 is allowed\n        }\n        return s[0] == '0';\n    }\n\n    private static long countPossibilities(char[] s) {\n        long count = 1;\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n            if (s[i] == '_') {\n                if (i == 0) {\n                    count *= 9; // can't be 0 for first digit\n                } else {\n                    count *= 10; // can be any digit\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        return count;\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.9\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.2186455882765586e-06, -4.494089080253616e-05, -4.6491513785440475e-06, 0.0, -7.629365427419543e-06, -2.7894584491150454e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.2755313036905136e-05, -4.386805812828243e-05, -1.7165990357170813e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -8.05822346592322e-05, -4.291525328881107e-06, -3.814689989667386e-06, -0.10056671500205994, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, -4.2914423829643056e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-06, 0.0, -4.410734163684538e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -2.50339189733495e-06, -2.8013790142722428e-05, -7.033323527139146e-06, -5.8412379075889476e-06, -1.883488948806189e-05, -1.07287787614041e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -4.768360213347478e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.0967194612021558e-05, -6.794906312279636e-06, -1.3708974620385561e-05, -8.22540732769994e-06, -4.291525328881107e-06, -7.033323527139146e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.00021705655672121793, -1.645074735279195e-05, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.2874520507466514e-05, -1.4066597032069694e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00012957210128661245, -5.960462772236497e-07, -4.529942543740617e-06, -1.9073468138230965e-06, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -4.410734163684538e-06, -2.145764938177308e-06, -2.062299427052494e-05, -5.125986263010418e-06, -5.483612312673358e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00032431588624604046, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0001234931987710297, -0.0009174905135296285, -0.03806241601705551, -2.884823152271565e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -0.005291622597724199, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.5491434931755066, -0.6963631510734558, -0.00016914